number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources> </patcit> <patcit ucid="JP-9149104-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country> <doc-number>9149104</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="X" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1199710A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ITO HIRONORI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NIPPON ELECTRIC CO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SERIZAWA MASAHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ITO, HIRONORI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NEC CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SERIZAWA, MASAHIRO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ITO HIRONORI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SERIZAWA MASAHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ITO, HIRONORI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SERIZAWA, MASAHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A voice decoding device smoothes the filter factor intermittently transmitted similarly to the RMS in decoding a voiceless section and feeds it to a synthesis filter, so that the discontinuous change of the filter factor due to the intermittent transmission can be prevented, and thereby the quality of decoded sound can be improved. To avoid influences of the filter factor and RMS transmitted in a past frame generated by the smoothing operation, the smoothing coefficient is determined so that the smoothing operation is not carried out during a predetermined time or predetermined frames after the decoding enters a voiceless section from a voice section or if the decoded feature parameter fulfills a predetermined condition.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention porte sur un décodeur vocal, lissant le facteur de filtrage transmis de manière intermittente au RMS, puis décodant la partie non vocale et la transmettant à un filtre synthétiseur afin de prévenir les variations discontinues du facteur de filtrage et améliorer la qualité du son décodé. Pour limiter l'influence du facteur de filtrage et du RMS transmis dans les trames précédentes et dû aux opérations de lissage, on fixe le coefficient de lissage pour que l'opération de lissage ne se fasse pas pendant un temps prédéterminé ni pendant des trames prédéterminées lorsque le décodage passe d'une partie vocale à une partie non vocale, ou si le paramètre de caractérisation décodé remplit une condition prédéterminée.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.or